WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.947
Citizen's toolkit.

00:00:01.897 --> 00:00:04.011
What you can actually do.

00:00:04.011 --> 00:00:06.511
You have read the investigations.

00:00:06.511 --> 00:00:10.272
You have seen the documented pattern of institutional capture.

00:00:10.272 --> 00:00:12.795
Now here is what you can do about it.

00:00:12.795 --> 00:00:20.090
This page provides seven concrete, legal, actionable tools that any Canadian citizen can use to hold the government accountable.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.443
You do not need to be a lawyer.

00:00:22.443 --> 00:00:24.954
You do not need to be a journalist.

00:00:24.954 --> 00:00:27.704
You do not need money or connections.

00:00:27.704 --> 00:00:32.227
You need the information documented on this site and the willingness to use it.

00:00:32.227 --> 00:00:35.352
These tools are your rights under Canadian law.

00:00:35.352 --> 00:00:38.170
The institutions may have been captured.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:42.999
But the law still provides mechanisms for citizens to act when institutions will not.

00:00:42.999 --> 00:00:46.863
Seven concrete actionable tools for any Canadian citizen.

00:00:46.863 --> 00:00:48.920
Why these tools matter.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:54.374
The system architecture documented across this site is designed to resist reform from within.

00:00:54.374 --> 00:00:56.909
Courts can't check power in time.

00:00:56.909 --> 00:00:59.511
Oversight bodies can't enforce.

00:00:59.511 --> 00:01:01.602
Media is captured.

00:01:01.602 --> 00:01:05.488
Pensions make everyone financially dependent on the status quo.

00:01:05.488 --> 00:01:08.647
Crown immunity shields the government from liability.

00:01:08.647 --> 00:01:12.477
But the law still provides tools for citizens to act directly.

00:01:12.477 --> 00:01:15.124
ATIP requests force disclosure.

00:01:15.124 --> 00:01:18.249
The lobbying registry reveals who benefits.

00:01:18.249 --> 00:01:21.829
MP communications create parliamentary records.

00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:27.068
Section five-oh-four private prosecution bypasses the Crown's refusal to prosecute itself.

00:01:27.068 --> 00:01:30.499
Oversight complaints create documented patterns.

00:01:30.499 --> 00:01:33.727
Sharing this site breaks the information monopoly.

00:01:33.727 --> 00:01:38.147
And voting with evidence rather than promises creates electoral accountability.

00:01:38.147 --> 00:01:41.204
None of these tools alone will change the system.

00:01:41.204 --> 00:01:47.022
All of them together, used by enough citizens, create pressure that captured institutions cannot absorb.

00:01:47.022 --> 00:01:49.590
The system depends on your inaction.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.863
These tools are your action.
